# ============================================================
# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# ============================================================

# === www → non-www canonical redirect (CRITICAL SEO fix) ===
# Prevents Google from indexing duplicate versions of every page.
# Before this, www.pokemonrandom.com/random-team/ and pokemonrandom.com/random-team/
# were both indexed with separate positions, splitting authority.
# Status 301 = permanent redirect (passes all link equity to canonical URL).
https://www.pokemonrandom.com/* https://pokemonrandom.com/:splat 301

# === forums subdomain → main site (PA=20 backlink preservation) ===
# forums.pokemonrandom.com was previously indexed by Moz with PA=20.
# Without a forums feature, redirect all traffic to the main site
# to preserve link equity and prevent 404s on backlinks pointing here.
https://forums.pokemonrandom.com/* https://pokemonrandom.com/:splat 301

# === Legacy WordPress-style feed URLs (Moz PA=15 backlink preservation) ===
# Old backlinks point to /03/214/feed/ and similar WordPress-style paths
# that no longer exist (Next.js static export uses /feed.xml).
# Redirect all such URLs to the actual RSS feed to preserve link equity.
/03/214/feed/  /feed.xml  301
/03/214/feed   /feed.xml  301
/03/*/feed/    /feed.xml  301
/feed/         /feed.xml  301
/feed          /feed.xml  301

# === Catch-all RSS/feed variants from legacy platforms ===
/*/*/feed/     /feed.xml  301
/*/*/feed      /feed.xml  301

# Note: We intentionally do NOT add a SPA-style rewrite (/* /index.html 200).
# This is a fully static export: every published URL is a real file, and
# Cloudflare Pages serves 404.html (with proper 404 status) for unknown paths.
# A catch-all rewrite to index.html would turn 404s into soft-404s (bad for SEO).
